WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:09.250
I stayed on at Woods Hole over the winter to purify 

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.890
the first motor of the kinesin super family,

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.450
which was a new motor protein at the time.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.230
We now know that kinesin is not one motor,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.400
but it's a large family of related motor proteins.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.580
For example,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.330
in humans,

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.030
they're 45 different genes encoding different kinesin motor 

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:29.820
proteins.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.580
And there's so many because they're involved in many different kinds of 

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.760
motor activities,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.620
not just axonal transport,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.720
which first motivated this study,

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.070
but a variety of other cargo transport and even activities 

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.400
in cell division, such as the construction of the mitotic spindle 

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.950
and the separation of chromosomes.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:59.000
These motility experiments really are what opened up the field.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.860
They first of all opened up the field by allowing us to be able to 

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.450
detect this activity of a motor protein 

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.660
that was critical for the subsequent purification.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.520
In many ways,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.220
the purification is technical.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:21.150
We had biochemical techniques that were already well established that 

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.310
we could use to go about and purify a protein.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:29.080
So these in vitro motility experiments really provided the 

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.800
foundation of being able to assay and detect the 

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.790
activity of a motor protein that we could then apply to the purification 

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.240
of kinesin.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.630
But it was much more than that;

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.050
these in vitro motility experiments,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.200
you know,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.010
kind of gave us this window into this life of what a motor 

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.880
protein is actually doing and how it might be working.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:00.250
It kind of gave us an experimental tool, that we just 

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:03.475
didn't have before, to study motility.

00:02:04.245 --> 00:02:04.505
I mean,

00:02:04.505 --> 00:02:08.385
before we could just look at cells with a microscope,

00:02:08.395 --> 00:02:12.375
a little bit helplessly, seeing all this motility going on,

00:02:12.545 --> 00:02:17.025
but not knowing really how to dissect it, or how to 

00:02:17.025 --> 00:02:21.655
understand it, or how to experimentally manipulate it. It was fascinating,

00:02:21.655 --> 00:02:22.405
of course,

00:02:22.995 --> 00:02:27.765
but we really couldn't get at the basic questions of how 

00:02:27.955 --> 00:02:29.805
these machines might actually work.

00:02:30.595 --> 00:02:34.855
These in vitro motility experiments essentially opened up a whole 

00:02:35.275 --> 00:02:39.005
new frontier of how we can measure motor proteins. 

